{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou","kind":"proposition","title":"Elementary symmetric polynomials in Jucys–Murphy elements are central in $H_n(q)$ with closed-form spectrum on each Wedderburn block","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-frobenius-self-duality-forces-lp-dual-extraction"],"cites":["references/murphy1992","references/jucys1974","references/kassel1995","references/mathas1999"],"tags":["jucys-murphy","central-element","hecke-algebra","wedderburn-block","cell-content","elementary-symmetric-polynomial","derived-coefficient"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.jm_esymm_central","text":"jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.md","leanSource":"jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou\"></a><p><em>In the Iwahori-Hecke algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(q)</code>, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_i^2 = (q - q^{-1})\\sigma_i + 1</code>, the multiplicative Jucys-Murphy elements</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  J_1 \\;=\\; 1, \\qquad J_{k+1} \\;=\\; \\sigma_k\\, J_k\\, \\sigma_k,\n  \\qquad k = 1, \\ldots, n-1,</code></pre>\n<p><em>commute with each other. The elementary symmetric polynomials</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  P_\\ell \\;:=\\; e_\\ell(J_1, J_2, \\ldots, J_n)\n  \\;\\in\\; Z\\bigl(H_n(q)\\bigr)</code></pre>\n<p><em>lie in the centre and act on the Wedderburn block <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_\\lambda</code> (for generic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>) as the scalar</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  c_\\ell(\\lambda) \\;=\\; e_\\ell\\!\\left(\\{q^{2c(\\square)} :\n    \\square \\in \\lambda\\}\\right)</code></pre>\n<p><em>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c(\\square) = j - i</code> is the content of cell <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\square = (i,j)</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.23.1","page":"b/prop-jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":79},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BraidKnot.jm_esymm_central","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
